{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0JvbGx5d29vZC8yMDE2LTIwMjAvQnVkZGhhJTIwaW4lMjBhJTIwVHJhZmZpYyUyMEphbSUyMCUyODIwMTYlMjkv","type":"movie","name":"Buddha in a Traffic Jam","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/bAia8POGJHaSLL9RCdo99ZNClKG.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/ehiMVFVHtgoGwyJ0cIXP3mmHe0N.jpg","description":"Vikram is a happy-go-lucky management student from a top Business School of India. He becomes an overnight sensation after a successful internet campaign against the radical fundamentalism of moral policing in India. This prompts his university teacher - Professor Ranjan Batki, to throw him a challenge for yet another internet campaign that would help raise money via a non-profit Pottery Club for poor people living in Maoists areas of India. Little does Vikram know that he is about to become a part of a plot that would risk his life and the nation. He gets entangled between two corrupt facets of India - Socialism and Capitalism, both of which are deeply rooted in India. It's a story inspired from true life incidents of Underbelly India.\n\nReleased 13 May 2016 · India · Language: Hindi · 114 min\nStudio: Friday Night Productions\n\nOn your server — Audio: Hindi","releaseInfo":"2016","genres":["Thriller","Crime","Bollywood"],"imdbRating":"6.7","runtime":"114 min","cast":["Anupam Kher","Arunoday Singh","Mahie Gill","Pallavi Joshi","Gopal Singh","Aanchal Dwivedi"],"director":["Vivek Agnihotri"],"released":"2016-05-13T00:00:00.000Z","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Vivek Agnihotri","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/tNsZQm6BKiK8Ejh8A9kPH4ZI4z6.jpg"},{"name":"Anupam Kher","character":"Professor Jamshed Batki","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/kgU5Ap1Kf9RnicB5DMcXEZqed2f.jpg"},{"name":"Arunoday Singh","character":"Vikram Pandit","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/tsiGIhjEwfR5SlKNsnl6VjocLoE.jpg"},{"name":"Mahie Gill","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/8BaceKKti